      "target": {
        "kind": "issue",
        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "title": "slug: not idempotent — slice after trailing-dash trim can re-introduce a trailing dash",
        "body": "`slug(value, fallback, maxLength)` in `src/repair/text-utils.ts:19` trims edge dashes and THEN `.slice(0, maxLength)`, so slicing on a `-` boundary re-introduces a trailing dash.\n\nRepro:\n```\nslug(\"a a\", \"x\", 2) === \"a-\"   // trailing dash\nslug(\"a-\", \"x\", 2)  === \"a\"    // => not idempotent: slug(slug(x)) !== slug(x)\n```\nFix: trim trailing dashes AFTER the length slice (or re-trim post-slice).",
